      "answer": "To save a checklist array to `localStorage`, you must first convert the array to a JSON string using `JSON.stringify()` before saving it with `localStorage.setItem(key, value)`. For restoration, retrieve the string using `localStorage.getItem(key)` and then parse it back into an array using `JSON.parse()`. \n\nExample:\n\n```javascript\n// Saving\nconst checklist = ['Item 1', 'Item 2'];\nlocalStorage.setItem('myChecklist', JSON.stringify(checklist));\n\n// Restoring\nconst savedString = localStorage.getItem('myChecklist');\nconst restoredArray = JSON.parse(savedString);\n```\n\n**Sources:**\n1. MDN Web Docs: [Window: localStorage property](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/localStorage)\n2. MDN Web Docs: [Storage: setItem() method](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage/setItem)"
